      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <omp.h>\n#include <climits>\n\nint main() {\n\tint n,s;\n\tstd::cin >> n >> s;\n\tstd::vector<std::vector<int> > matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\n\tfor(int i=0;i<n;i++)\n\t\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) \n\t\t\tscanf(\"%d\", &(matrix[i][j]));\n\n\tassert(s<n);\n\tassert(n<8000);\n\tassert(s>0);\n\tassert(n>0);\n\n\t// Build 2D prefix sum (integral image)\n\tstd::vector<std::vector<long long>> pref(n+1, std::vector<long long>(n+1, 0));\n\t#pragma omp parallel for schedule(static) collapse(2)\n\tfor(int i=1; i<=n; ++i) {\n\t\tfor(int j=1; j<=n; ++j) {\n\t\t\tpref[i][j] = matrix[i-1][j-1] + pref[i-1][j] + pref[i][j-1] - pref[i-1][j-1];\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tint mxSum = INT_MIN;\n\t#pragma omp parallel for reduction(max:mxSum) schedule(static) collapse(2)\n\tfor(int i=0; i<=n-s; ++i) {\n\t\tfor(int j=0; j<=n-s; ++j) {\n\t\t\tlong long sum = pref[i+s][j+s] - pref[i][j+s] - pref[i+s][j] + pref[i][j];\n\t\t\tif(sum > mxSum) mxSum = (int)sum;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tprintf(\"%d\\n\",mxSum);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Use OpenMP work sharing via #pragma omp parallel for collapse(2) reduction(max:mxSum) schedule(static) on integral image submatrix sum queries to achieve better load balance and lower scheduling overhead compared to runtime/dynamic scheduling. The prefix-sum construction is also parallelized with static scheduling, ensuring even thread granularity across both phases.",
  "notes": "Replaces the sequential sliding-window algorithm with a two-dimensional prefix sum (integral image) approach. Both the O(N^2) prefix computation and the O((N-S+1)^2) search are fully parallelized using OpenMP work-sharing constructs, reduction for max, and static scheduling to minimize runtime overhead.",
